---
title: Bolognese Sauce
servings: 6
prep time: 30 minutes
cook time: 3 hours
tags:
  - dinner
  - meat
  - sauce
  - long
  - medium
---
In a #pot{}, melt @pancetta{150%g} with @olive oil{3%tbsp} for a few minutes at 
medium-low heat.

Add minced @carrots{60%g}, @celery{60%g}, and @onion{60%g} until softened but 
not browned.

Remove from pot and put into a bowl on the side.

Raise temperature to medium heat, then add @ground beef{400%g}, break it up, 
and cook for ~{10%minutes} to where most of the liquid has rendered out entirely
browned. 

Add @tomato paste{1%tbsp} and mix in for a few more minutes. Add @milk{0.25%cup}
to tenderize the meat.

Add optional @red wine{0.5%cup} until evaporated. 

Add back the minced mirepoix and cook for a few more minutes.

Add @stock{1%cup} of your choice and @strained tomatoes{200%g} and set heat back
to simmer. 

Cook for ~{2-2:30%hours} or longer. Half way through, add @milk{0.25%cup}.

Season with salt and pepper before serving.
